ry":"One of the Levites who took part in praising God on the removal of the ark to Jerusalem (1 Chr. 16:5).","verses":4,"father":"","mother":"","v":[5]},{"id":"eliab_1077","name":"Eliab","also":"","summary":"Lyre player.","verses":3,"father":"","mother":"","v":[5]},{"id":"jehiel_770","name":"Jehiel","also":"","summary":"One of the Levites “of the second degree,” appointed to conduct the music on the occasion of the ark’s being removed to Jerusalem (1 Chr. 15:18, 20).","verses":3,"father":"","mother":"","v":[5]},{"id":"shemiramoth_2651","name":"Shemiramoth","also":"","summary":"A Levite in David’s time (1 Chr. 15:18, 20).","verses":3,"father":"","mother":"","v":[5]},{"id":"jahaziel_697","name":"Jahaziel","also":"","summary":"A priest who accompanied the removal of the ark to Jerusalem (1 Chr. 16:6).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[6]},{"id":"israel_682","name":"Israel","also":"","summary":"One who follows on another’s heels; supplanter, (Gen. 25:26; 27:36; Hos. 12:2-4), the second born of the twin sons of Isaac by Rebekah. He was born probably at Lahai-roi, when his father was fifty-nine and Abraham one hundred and fifty-nine years old.","verses":1009,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[13,17]},{"id":"abraham_58","name":"Abraham","also":"Abram","summary":"Father of a multitude, son of Terah, named (Gen. 11:27) before his older brothers Nahor and Haran, because he was the heir of the promises. Till the age of seventy, Abram sojourned among his kindred in his native country of Chaldea.","verses":277,"father":"Terah","mother":"","v":[16]},{"id":"isaac_616","name":"Isaac","also":"","summary":"The only son of Abraham by Sarah. He was the longest lived of the three patriarchs (Gen. 21:1-3).","verses":123,"father":"Abraham","mother":"Sarah","v":[16]},{"id":"canaan_914","name":"Canaan","also":"Canaanites, Canaanite","summary":"The fourth son of Ham (Gen. 10:6). His descendants were under a curse in consequence of the transgression of his father (9:22-27). His eldest son, Zidon, was the father of the Sidonians and Phoenicians.","verses":84,"father":"Ham","mother":"","v":[18]},{"id":"jeduthun_1224","name":"Jeduthun","also":"Ethan","summary":"A Levite of the family of Merari, one of the leaders of the temple music (1 Chr. 6:44; 15:17, 19). He was probably the same as Jeduthun.","verses":13,"father":"Kishi","mother":"","v":[38,41,42]},{"id":"hosah_1554","name":"Hosah","also":"","summary":"A Levite of the family of Merari (1 Chr. 16:38).","verses":4,"father":"","mother":"","v":[38]},{"id":"zadok_2973","name":"Zadok","also":"","summary":"A son of Ahitub, of the line of Eleazer (2 Sam. 8:17; 1 Chr. 24:3), high priest in the time of David (2 Sam. 20:25) and Solomon (1 Kings 4:4).","verses":40,"father":"Ahitub","mother":"","v":[39]},{"id":"heman_1490","name":"Heman","also":"","summary":"Grandson of Samuel (1 Chr. 6:33; 15:17), to whom the 88th Psalm probably was inscribed.","verses":12,"father":"Joel","mother":"","v":[41,42]}],"places":[{"id":"canaan_272","name":"Canaan","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":31.69353,"lon":34.84388,"summary":"The country which derived its name from the preceding. The name as first used by the Phoenicians denoted only the maritime plain on which Sidon was built.","verses":76,"v":[18]},{"id":"gibeon_470","name":"Gibeon","kind":"City","lat":31.84668,"lon":35.1852,"summary":"Hill-city, “one of the royal cities, greater than Ai, and all the men thereof were mighty” (Josh. 10:2). Its inhabitants were Hivites (11:19).","verses":35,"v":[39]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[935,935,935,727,727,430,430,3322,3322,8432,8432,168,168,834,1732,5186,5186,0,0,7126,7126,7126,5930,5930,8002,8002,8002,6440,430],[1732,1732,3615,3615,5927,5930,5930,5930,8002,8002,8002,1288,1288,5971,5971,8034,8034,8034,3068,3068,3068],[2505,2505,2505,3605,3605,376,5704,802,3478,3478,3603,3603,3899,3899,829,829,829,809,809,809,809],[5414,5414,4480,4480,3881,3881,8334,8334,6440,727,727,3068,3068,3